&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;resize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;centerOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;active&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;centerOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;frame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/body&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/html&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The parts worth reading in the demo:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// a tiny spring: same feel as Framer Motion's useSpring({ stiffness: 380, damping: 26 })&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;speed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;abs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;              &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// px per second&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;w&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;66&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;min&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;92&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;speed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;        &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// faster = longer drop&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;52&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;min&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;speed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;90&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;       &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...and a little thinner&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;w&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;min&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;W&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;w&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;spring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// keep the drop inside the bar&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lensIn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`translate(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;M&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;px, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;M&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;px) scale(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;M&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;)`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The demo adds three things the shipped component doesn't have:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drag along the bar and the lens follows your finger to the nearest tab, stretching over every tab it passes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It clamps the drop inside the bar, because a 158px drop on the last tab hangs off the edge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With &lt;code&gt;prefers-reduced-motion: reduce&lt;/code&gt; it jumps straight to the new tab, with no stretch and no wobble. Do that in anything you ship. A drop that stretches across the screen is exactly the kind of motion that setting is for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Easy ways to get it wrong
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Scaling the copy around its own centre.&lt;/strong&gt; The magnified icon drifts sideways as the lens moves. Use &lt;code&gt;transform-origin: 0 0&lt;/code&gt; and put the whole offset in the translate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A CSS transition on the lens width.&lt;/strong&gt; The width then lags behind the position. Set width, height and transform in the same frame, all read from the spring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A focusable copy.&lt;/strong&gt; Keyboard users tab through ten tabs instead of five. Mark the copy &lt;code&gt;aria-hidden&lt;/code&gt; and give every button in it &lt;code&gt;tabindex="-1"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Labels inside the lens.&lt;/strong&gt; They get cut by the lens edge. Hide them in the copy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About me, and the links.&lt;/strong&gt; I'm Teodor, and I make animated UI components at qodesign. The tab bar in this post is one of them, so this is partly a post about my own product. The demo above is MIT: copy it, change it, ship it. The full component adds the orb that turns into a full-screen player, the compact bar on scroll, the badge pop, a React + TypeScript + Tailwind + Framer Motion version, and a PROMPT.md for AI coding tools. It's &lt;a href="https://qodesign.dev/components/tabbar-liquid?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=tutorial&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tabbar_lens" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;$3 on qodesign.dev&lt;/a&gt;. This week I'm also putting a few components on GitHub for free (MIT): two dashboards, a toast stack, a pricing switch and an upload dropzone. I'll add the link here when the repo is public.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you build a lens with a real displacement map that works in Safari, I'd like to see it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I wrote this post with help from an AI assistant. The code excerpts are copied from the shipped component, and the demo was run and checked in a browser before publishing.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A Persian document often contains much more than Persian prose: English terminology, code, links, tables and mathematical notation all have to coexist. &lt;strong&gt;NilaMarkdown Editor&lt;/strong&gt; is my project for editing and viewing that kind of mixed RTL/LTR document.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F7wx7e990iuc83qivyojj.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F7wx7e990iuc83qivyojj.png" alt="NilaMarkdown live editor" width="800" height="450"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it does
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The editor provides a rich editing surface, a Markdown source mode and a searchable, collapsible document outline. The outline is intended to make long documents easier to navigate in both rendered and source views.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The supported content includes tables, task lists, blockquotes, footnotes, math, fenced code and Mermaid diagrams. Persian/RTL and English/LTR support are part of the document workflow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For React applications, the package exposes separate editor and viewer entry points. The viewer entry does not load ProseMirror or the editing tools, while both components share the Markdown parser and related document logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try the local demo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Requirements: &lt;strong&gt;Node.js 20+ and pnpm 11&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone https://github.com/mnikoie/NilaMarkdown-Editor.git
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd &lt;/span&gt;NilaMarkdown-Editor
pnpm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install
&lt;/span&gt;pnpm dev
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;code&gt;http://localhost:3000/markdown&lt;/code&gt; for the editor or &lt;code&gt;/viewer&lt;/code&gt; for the lightweight viewer. This is a source repository with a Next.js demo; I am not announcing a hosted editor service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The repository also includes a Windows launcher, package usage examples and commands for type checking, unit tests and Playwright tests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The feedback I need
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mixed-direction documents have plenty of edge cases. If the editor mishandles heading navigation, source/rendered synchronization or a particular combination of Persian and English, a small reproducible document would be useful.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please include your browser version, the steps you took and what you expected. Use a synthetic sample rather than uploading private documents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/mnikoie/NilaMarkdown-Editor" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Source, screenshots and setup guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; · &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/mnikoie/NilaMarkdown-Editor/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Report a problem or suggest a feature&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Disclosure: this introduction was prepared with AI assistance from the published project documentation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A post on our blog gets read by at least three kinds of client. People read it in a browser. Search crawlers want the text in the HTML, plus some structured data. And Medium's import tool, which we use to syndicate posts, fetches the page remotely and has to find the images by itself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We're building &lt;a href="https://motion-lab.io" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MotionLab&lt;/a&gt;, personalized stretching and mobility sessions. Earlier posts in this series covered our AI session builder, our Postgres push queue, and billing. This one is about the blog. Posts are stored as TypeScript data. A small parser turns plain strings into typed blocks, and that one parse feeds the rendered page, the JSON-LD and the metadata. It also covers the two fixes it took before Medium imports kept our images.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stack: Next.js 16.2 (App Router), React 19.2, TypeScript. There's no Markdown or MDX library in &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt;; the formatting rules live in one file, &lt;code&gt;src/lib/content/blog-format.ts&lt;/code&gt;. Snippets are trimmed from the real code; &lt;code&gt;// ...&lt;/code&gt; marks cuts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Posts are data, publishing is a commit
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every post is an entry in a &lt;code&gt;Record&lt;/code&gt; keyed by slug, in the route file itself:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PostData&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;readTime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;metaDescription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;heroImage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;heroAlt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;keyTakeaways&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;sections&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;heading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;POSTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Record&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PostData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;publishedBlogSlugs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;keys&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;POSTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;generateStaticParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;publishedBlogSlugs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;slug&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;slug&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;generateStaticParams&lt;/code&gt; lists every key, so Next.js can prerender each post at build time. &lt;code&gt;sitemap.ts&lt;/code&gt; imports &lt;code&gt;publishedBlogSlugs&lt;/code&gt;, so a new key lands in the sitemap without a second edit. There's no CMS and no database read at request time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each section's &lt;code&gt;content&lt;/code&gt; is a plain string with a few Markdown-like conventions. One section of our desk neck-stretch post, for example, is an intro paragraph, a blank line, then numbered steps written like &lt;code&gt;1. Chin tuck: Look straight ahead and gently slide your chin straight back...&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. First, put the article in the HTML
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The root layout wraps every page in a &lt;code&gt;ClientOnly&lt;/code&gt; component. This is what it used to look like:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Renders AuthProvider only on the client — prevents Firebase SDK from running during SSR/build&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;dynamic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ssr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ClientOnly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The intent was to keep the auth SDK out of server rendering. The side effect was that &lt;code&gt;children&lt;/code&gt;, meaning every page, sat inside a component that never renders on the server. Anything that read our raw HTML without running JavaScript got none of the page content.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/code&gt; subscribes to auth state in a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; and copies the user, profile and subscription state into Zustand stores. It doesn't provide React context, so it never needed to wrap anything:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// The auth listener stays client-only. Children render on the server so public&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// pages, including the blog, are in the HTML.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;dynamic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ssr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ClientOnly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The listener still only runs in the browser, and the pages render on the server. If a client-only provider wraps your whole tree, check whether it really needs to be a wrapper.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. A parser with a small grammar
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The parser's output is a small union type:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Block&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;inlines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Inline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Inline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[][]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;ol&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Inline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[][]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;figure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;credit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;parseBlocks&lt;/code&gt; splits the content on blank lines, trims each line, and hands each chunk to &lt;code&gt;parseLines&lt;/code&gt;, which tries a fixed list of rules in order:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A chunk whose first line is exactly &lt;code&gt;![alt](src)&lt;/code&gt; becomes a &lt;code&gt;figure&lt;/code&gt;, either on its own or followed by an italic credit line like &lt;code&gt;*Photo: Unsplash*&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A chunk where every line is a &lt;code&gt;-&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;*&lt;/code&gt; bullet becomes a &lt;code&gt;ul&lt;/code&gt;. Two or more lines that are all numbered become an &lt;code&gt;ol&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A chunk that starts with a bold label can become an &lt;code&gt;h3&lt;/code&gt;, with the rest as a paragraph or a list under it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A single line shaped like &lt;code&gt;1. Chin tuck: Look straight ahead...&lt;/code&gt; becomes an &lt;code&gt;h3&lt;/code&gt; ("1. Chin tuck") plus a paragraph.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anything else is one paragraph, with its lines joined by spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The bold-label rule is the fussiest, because plenty of sentences start with bold text without being headings:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;headingFromLine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;line&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;heading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;full&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;line&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\*\*([^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;)\*\*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;$/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;full&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;heading&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;cleanHeading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;full&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;heading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;heading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;120&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;heading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lead&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;line&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\*\*([^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;)\*\*([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;:.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]?)\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;.*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;$/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;numbered&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\d{1,2}\.\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\S&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;question&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;endsWith&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;numbered&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;punct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;question&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;numbered&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;punct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;question&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;a-z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;heading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;cleanHeading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A bold line on its own is a heading. A bold lead-in only counts when the label ends with a colon or period (inside or just outside the &lt;code&gt;**&lt;/code&gt;), is numbered, or is a question. So &lt;code&gt;**When to see a professional.** Stretching is...&lt;/code&gt; gets a heading, but &lt;code&gt;**Runners** are the most common...&lt;/code&gt; stays a sentence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Inline parsing is one regex for bold, italic and links. A link only becomes a link if its href passes &lt;code&gt;safeHref&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;safeHref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startsWith&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startsWith&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;//&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;protocol&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;protocol&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;http:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Site-relative paths and http(s) URLs pass. Protocol-relative &lt;code&gt;//host&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;javascript:&lt;/code&gt; don't, and those fall back to plain text. &lt;code&gt;BlogProse&lt;/code&gt; renders the blocks as ordinary React elements, so the article body gets React's normal escaping and never goes through &lt;code&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. The same parse, as structured data
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because the content is already typed blocks, structured data doesn't need a second pass over the raw text. &lt;code&gt;faqsFromSections&lt;/code&gt; collects question headings (section headings or &lt;code&gt;h3&lt;/code&gt;s ending in &lt;code&gt;?&lt;/code&gt;) and pairs each with the first paragraph under it. Answers under 40 characters are skipped, long ones are capped at 500, and fewer than two questions means no FAQ at all. &lt;code&gt;howToFromSections&lt;/code&gt; looks for numbered &lt;code&gt;h3&lt;/code&gt; steps followed by a paragraph, and keeps the section with the most steps if it has at least three.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;buildBlogGraph&lt;/code&gt; always emits a &lt;code&gt;BlogPosting&lt;/code&gt; and a &lt;code&gt;BreadcrumbList&lt;/code&gt;, and adds &lt;code&gt;FAQPage&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;HowTo&lt;/code&gt; when those helpers find something. The page writes the graph into a script tag:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;jsonLd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&amp;lt;/g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;u003c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"application/ld+json"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;__html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;jsonLd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;graph&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;JSON.stringify&lt;/code&gt; doesn't escape &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/code&gt;, so a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; in a title or answer would close the tag early. &lt;code&gt;\u003c&lt;/code&gt; parses back to the same JSON.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One caveat before you invest in FAQ and HowTo markup: &lt;a href="https://developers.google.com/search/blog/2023/08/howto-faq-changes" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Google changed both in 2023&lt;/a&gt;. FAQ rich results now only show for "well-known, authoritative government and health websites", and HowTo rich results were deprecated. Google also says unused structured data "does not cause problems". Ours comes out of a parse the page already does, so it's cheap to keep, but don't expect it to change how your results look.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Titles and descriptions from the same fields
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our post titles run long, and the root layout has a &lt;code&gt;"%s | MotionLab"&lt;/code&gt; title template. &lt;code&gt;seoTitle&lt;/code&gt; builds the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;title&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; from the title's first clause:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;primaryPhrase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;cut&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;split&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\s\|\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\s[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;–—&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;].&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;cut&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\([^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\)\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*/g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+/g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;seoTitle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;primaryPhrase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;18&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\([^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\)\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;*/g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+/g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BRAND&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BRAND&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;trimAtWord&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phrase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BRAND&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BRAND&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;"Power Training and Mobility: Why the Two Go Together (And How to Balance Both)" becomes "Power Training and Mobility | MotionLab". When it has to truncate, &lt;code&gt;trimAtWord&lt;/code&gt; cuts at a space and drops trailing words like "to" and "the". &lt;code&gt;generateMetadata&lt;/code&gt; passes the result as &lt;code&gt;title: { absolute: title }&lt;/code&gt;, which skips the layout template so the brand doesn't appear twice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;metaDescription&lt;/code&gt; works the same way for descriptions: keep it if it fits in 160 characters, otherwise cut at the last sentence end after character 100, then at a clause break, and only then at a word.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  6. Getting Medium's importer to keep the images
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Medium's help center says the import tool hands the URL to a &lt;a href="https://help.medium.com/hc/en-us/articles/360033931713-Trouble-importing-content-using-the-import-tool" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;third-party service&lt;/a&gt; that returns the page's contents "to the best of their ability". Our images needed two fixes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fix one: absolute URLs, plain &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;img&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;next/image&lt;/code&gt; renders a relative &lt;code&gt;/_next/image?url=...&lt;/code&gt; optimizer URL, and our content uses root-relative paths like &lt;code&gt;/images/blog/...&lt;/code&gt;. Both only work if the reader resolves them against our domain, and the optimizer URL also depends on our image endpoint. Now every image source goes through one helper:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://motion-lab.io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Blog images must render with absolute URLs so off-site importers&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// (Medium's medium.com/p/import, RSS readers, scrapers) can fetch them.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Relative paths resolve the same way a browser would on /blog/&amp;lt;slug&amp;gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;absoluteUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/blog/`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;With &lt;code&gt;/blog/&lt;/code&gt; as the base, &lt;code&gt;/images/a.jpg&lt;/code&gt; resolves to &lt;code&gt;https://motion-lab.io/images/a.jpg&lt;/code&gt; and a bare &lt;code&gt;img.jpg&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;/blog/img.jpg&lt;/code&gt;, as a browser would on &lt;code&gt;/blog/&amp;lt;slug&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. The same helper feeds &lt;code&gt;og:image&lt;/code&gt;, the Twitter card and the JSON-LD &lt;code&gt;image&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fix two: no &lt;code&gt;loading="lazy"&lt;/code&gt; on body images.&lt;/strong&gt; The first fix used a plain &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;img loading="lazy"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Two days later we took the attribute off body images:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;figure&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;index&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"my-8"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"relative w-full aspect-[3/2] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-ml-border"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* Plain &amp;lt;img&amp;gt; with an absolute src (not next/image's /_next/image URL)
        so Medium imports and other off-site readers can fetch it.
        No loading="lazy": Medium's importer drops lazy images. */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* eslint-disable-next-line @next/next/no-img-element */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;img&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;absoluteUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;block&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;block&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;decoding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"async"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* ... */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;figure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The hero image gets the same treatment, with &lt;code&gt;fetchPriority="high"&lt;/code&gt; and no &lt;code&gt;loading&lt;/code&gt; attribute. The trade-off is real: blog pages no longer get &lt;code&gt;next/image&lt;/code&gt; resizing or the AVIF/WebP formats our &lt;code&gt;next.config.ts&lt;/code&gt; enables for the optimizer. Browsers get the original files, which in our posts are almost all JPEGs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  7. Related reading without a database
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The links at the bottom of a post come from &lt;code&gt;POSTS&lt;/code&gt; too. &lt;code&gt;relatedReading&lt;/code&gt; sorts the slugs in the post's category alphabetically and walks outward from the current one, alternating next and previous, until it has five. Then it adds up to two guides whose keywords appear in the slug or title. It's deterministic: the same build always produces the same links.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Wrapping up
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check that your content is in the server HTML before tuning anything else. A client-only wrapper around &lt;code&gt;children&lt;/code&gt; can quietly take it out.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When one team writes all the content, a small grammar you own can be enough. Keep the rules next to the parser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parse once into typed blocks, then derive the page, the JSON-LD and the metadata from them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escape &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/code&gt; in inline JSON-LD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If other services import your pages, give them absolute image URLs and plain &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;img&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tags, and watch out for &lt;code&gt;loading="lazy"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can see the output on the &lt;a href="https://motion-lab.io/blog" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MotionLab blog&lt;/a&gt;: view source on any post for the server-rendered HTML and the JSON-LD.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do you hand-roll formatting like this, or reach for MDX or remark? And if you syndicate to Medium, what else have you found its importer drops? Tell us in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This post was drafted with AI assistance and reviewed by the MotionLab team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ever spent three hours tracing a single &lt;code&gt;NullPointerException&lt;/code&gt; across five different microservices? You grep through endless terminal windows, match timestamps, and manually piece together the puzzle. It’s exhausting.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a full-stack developer working heavily with Spring Boot, I realized that while microservices solve scalability issues, they introduce a massive debugging headache. I wanted a tool that didn't just &lt;em&gt;show&lt;/em&gt; me the logs, but actually &lt;em&gt;helped&lt;/em&gt; me fix them in real-time. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since I couldn't find a lightweight, developer-friendly solution that fit my exact needs, I built one. Meet &lt;strong&gt;LogIQ&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What is LogIQ? 🧠
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgodg0hes370yj5hvwdwk.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgodg0hes370yj5hvwdwk.png" alt=" " width="799" height="335"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/shan2003034/logiq-backend" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LogIQ&lt;/a&gt; is a centralized observability SaaS platform and a custom Java SDK designed to streamline the debugging workflow. It captures telemetry data, tracks server health in real-time, and uses an AI Neural Engine to analyze complex stack traces and provide actionable code fixes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of navigating through different log files, everything is streamed directly into a modern, cyber-tech inspired dashboard.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Core Features at a Glance:
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Plug-and-Play SDK:&lt;/strong&gt; A custom Spring Boot starter that integrates in under 2 minutes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Real-Time Health Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt; Zero-lag live server status tracking via WebSockets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;AI-Powered Debugging:&lt;/strong&gt; Instant stack-trace analysis and fix suggestions powered by LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Secure Team Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Built-in Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to manage Owner/Developer access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Cyber-Tech UI:&lt;/strong&gt; A sleek Glassmorphism interface built with React, Tailwind CSS, and Framer Motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Architecture: How It All Fits Together 🏗️
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted LogIQ to have zero performance bottleneck on the host microservices. To achieve this, I separated the system into three main components:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt; &lt;strong&gt;The Client SDK (&lt;code&gt;logiq-spring-boot-starter&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; Runs on the target microservices, collecting logs and health metrics asynchronously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; &lt;strong&gt;The Core Engine (Spring Boot Backend):&lt;/strong&gt; Acts as the secure broker, handling JWT authentication, database persistence (MySQL), and routing messages to the AI provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; &lt;strong&gt;The Dashboard (React Frontend):&lt;/strong&gt; Consumes REST APIs and listens to WebSocket channels for live updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the high-level system architecture:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;flowchart TB
    subgraph Target Microservices
        S1["Spring Boot App 1&amp;lt;br/&amp;gt;(LogIQ SDK)"]
        S2["Spring Boot App 2&amp;lt;br/&amp;gt;(LogIQ SDK)"]
    end

    subgraph LogIQ Core Server
        API["REST APIs&amp;lt;br/&amp;gt;(Auth, Projects)"]
        WS["WebSocket Broker&amp;lt;br/&amp;gt;(STOMP)"]
        AI["AI Processing Engine"]
    end

    subgraph Client Browser
        UI["React Dashboard&amp;lt;br/&amp;gt;(Tailwind + Framer Motion)"]
    end

    S1 --&amp;gt;|"Async Telemetry Stream"| API
    S2 --&amp;gt;|"Async Telemetry Stream"| API

    API &amp;lt;--&amp;gt; AI
    API --&amp;gt;|"Publish Events"| WS
    WS --&amp;gt;|"Real-time Health &amp;amp; Logs"| UI&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


  Building the Custom Spring Boot SDK 📦
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of the most exciting parts of this project was building my own custom SDK. I wanted the integration process to be frictionless for other developers. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By creating a custom &lt;code&gt;spring-boot-starter&lt;/code&gt;, a developer only needs to add a single dependency to their &lt;code&gt;pom.xml&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight xml"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;dependency&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;groupId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;com.bytecodelk&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/groupId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;artifactId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;logiq-spring-boot-starter&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/artifactId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;version&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;1.0.0&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/version&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/dependency&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then, simply configure the project credentials in &lt;code&gt;application.properties&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight properties"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;logiq.api.key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;YOUR_PROJECT_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;logiq.server.url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;http://localhost:8080&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Behind the scenes, the SDK automatically hooks into the Spring environment, intercepts application exceptions, and pushes them to the LogIQ backend asynchronously so it never slows down the main application thread.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Magic: Real-Time WebSockets &amp;amp; AI Analysis 🪄
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Zero-Lag Telemetry
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of relying on heavy polling mechanisms, I implemented &lt;strong&gt;WebSockets (STOMP)&lt;/strong&gt; in the Spring Boot backend. When the backend receives a new log entry or health ping from the SDK, it broadcasts the payload to a specific project topic. The React frontend listens to this topic and updates the UI instantly. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. The AI Neural Engine
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reading a 50-line Java stack trace is never fun. In the LogIQ dashboard, if an error is flagged as critical, you can click &lt;strong&gt;"Analyze with AI"&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Spring Boot backend securely formats a strict prompt containing the exact stack trace and context, sends it to the LLM via an API call, and returns a human-readable explanation and code fix. It ensures that sensitive environment variables are not unnecessarily exposed, keeping the debugging process secure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  &lt;iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/JlSOAo2mxvI" width="710" height="399"&gt;
  &lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Frontend: Cyber-Tech Aesthetics 🌌
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers stare at screens all day, so the UI had to be easy on the eyes but visually striking. I opted for a dark-themed, industrial cyber-tech aesthetic. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using &lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Tailwind CSS&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Framer Motion&lt;/strong&gt;, I built a responsive Glassmorphism UI. I even integrated &lt;strong&gt;React Three Fiber&lt;/strong&gt; to render some subtle 3D depth elements on the landing page to give it that futuristic command-center feel.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Conclusion &amp;amp; Next Steps
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building LogIQ has been an incredible journey that pushed my boundaries in full-stack development, API design, and real-time data handling. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently, the SDK is exclusively available for &lt;strong&gt;Spring Boot&lt;/strong&gt;, but I plan to expand support to Node.js and Python microservices in the near future. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you are a developer looking for an easier way to debug your distributed systems, or just curious about the code, I'd love for you to check it out! &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🔗 &lt;strong&gt;Check out the source code on GitHub:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;a href="https://github.com/shan2003034/logiq-backend" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LogIQ Backend Repository&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;a href="https://github.com/shan2003034/logiq-frontend" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LogIQ Frontend Repository&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you find the architecture interesting or the tool helpful, please consider dropping a ⭐️ on the repositories. I’m also open to feedback, contributions, and ideas for new features!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What’s your current go-to strategy for debugging microservices? Let me know in the comments below! 👇&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  softwareengineering #springboot #reactjs #microservices #ai #webdevelopment #opensource
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Good React form components share one anatomy: a label tied to the control, one message row that shows the hint or the error, and a counter when there is a limit, with the ids and aria attributes wired for you. Connect them to react-hook-form with register for native inputs and Controller for everything else, and validate with one zod schema once a field has been left. On phones, every control needs 16px text, the right keypad, 44px targets and a bottom sheet instead of a popover.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every product ships the same handful of forms: sign up, checkout, settings, a filter panel, a support request. The controls differ, the bugs repeat. A label that is not tied to its input, an error that shows up only as a red border, a date picker that opens a small popover under your thumb, a custom select that the browser's autofill skips. This guide treats React form components as one set: which controls a product needs, the anatomy they should share, how to wire them to react-hook-form and zod, and what each one should do on a phone. The examples use Wingo UI, the library we build, so we are not neutral; outside facts link to their sources and are dated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Which form controls does a product actually need?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fifteen kinds of input in the table below cover the forms most products ship. Pick each one by what the person is entering, then check what it does on a phone. Most React input components look alike on a desktop. They split apart at 390px, where a popover has no room and a 32px target is too small for a thumb.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What people enter&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Component&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;On a phone&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Short text, email, URL&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/input" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Input&lt;/a&gt; (Free)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;16px text, keypad from the &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt;, 44px box&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Long text&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/textarea" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Textarea&lt;/a&gt; (Free)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Grows line by line, return makes a new line&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One of 2 to 5 visible options&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/radio-group" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Radio Group&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/segmented-control" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Segmented Control&lt;/a&gt; (Free)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;44px targets, a radio's whole row is one&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One of a known list&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
